Hi,

I currently have a working app that uses Leaflet and has an absolutePanel with controls for toggling different map layers. I started this project by cannibalizing from Joe Cheng's amazing SuperZip app.

I have a problem born out of wanting to show a rendered DataTable on a certain map view. The table successfully shows and hides based on user inputs, but it permanently impacts the size of the absolutePanel. In other words, when I first start my App - my panel is the perfect, slim size. When I select the requisite buttons to display the table, the panel widens to accomodate it. When I de-select those items, the table goes away, but the panel remains the same widened size.

Anyone have any advice for how to best handle this situation?

One solution I have played around with is simply displaying a SECOND absolutePanel dedicated to displaying this table, and nesting a conditionalPanel inside of it. However, I run into the same issue. When the data is displayed, it successfully appears in a large box over my map. When the table goes away, the large box remains and obstructs the view.

I suspect there is another method of tackling this situation that I'm not seeing. I don't have much CSS experience, and I'm using what the SuperZip explorer came with.

Here's a snippet of the code I am usingthat renders a datatable that permanently increases the panel's size.

absolutePanel(id = "controls", class = "panel panel-default", fixed = TRUE,
        draggable = TRUE, top = 60, left = "auto", right = 20, bottom = "auto",
        width = "auto", height = "auto",

        h2("Lives Explorer"),

        radioButtons("view", "View:", views, selected = "Map Only"),
        hr(),

        conditionalPanel(condition="input.view=='Lives'",
          radioButtons("lob", "LoB:", lob_vars, selected = "ma"),
          checkboxGroupInput("strat", "Stratification:", strats, selected = "Traditional"),
          radioButtons("thresh", "Follow-up year Threshold:", thresholds, selected = "None"),
          DT::dataTableOutput("matrix"),
          hr(),
          DT::dataTableOutput("ppv")

Here's my attempt at a second panel, which obstructively lingers when the table is displayed, then hidden.

      absolutePanel(id = "controls", class = "panel panel-default", fixed = TRUE,
                    draggable = TRUE, top = "auto", left = "auto", right = 20, bottom = 20,
                    width = "auto", height = "auto",

                    conditionalPanel(condition="input.view=='Lives'",
                                     DT::dataTableOutput("matrix"),
                                     hr(),
                                     DT::dataTableOutput("ppv"))

      ),

And here's the css supporting both:

#controls {
  /* Appearance */
  background-color: white;
  padding: 0 20px 20px 20px;
  cursor: move;
  /* Fade out while not hovering */
  opacity: 0.65;
  zoom: 0.9;
  transition: opacity 500ms 1s;
}
#controls:hover {
  /* Fade in while hovering */
  opacity: 0.95;
  transition-delay: 0;
}

